nl80211: a scan result's boot-clock age only where the kernel's own agrees

Carried by Kryptik against wpa_supplicant 2.12; not upstream at the time of
writing, and hostap's main branch has the same code. The kernel gives each
BSS two ages: NL80211_BSS_SEEN_MS_AGO, which it counts itself, and
NL80211_BSS_LAST_SEEN_BOOTTIME, a stamp on the machine's boot clock that
wpa_supplicant subtracts from its own CLOCK_BOOTTIME. In a time namespace
that clock is offset from the machine's and the kernel does not translate the
stamp, so every scan result reads as old as the offset, hours or days. The
BSS table then drops each entry at its next expiry pass (bss_expiration_age,
180 s), within ten seconds of the scan that found it.

The stamp's age is now taken only when it agrees with SEEN_MS_AGO within a
second, or when the kernel sends no SEEN_MS_AGO. Outside a time namespace the
two agree, and nothing changes.

--- a/src/drivers/driver_nl80211_scan.c
+++ b/src/drivers/driver_nl80211_scan.c
@@ -857,7 +857,7 @@
 	if (bss[NL80211_BSS_SEEN_MS_AGO])
 		r->age = nla_get_u32(bss[NL80211_BSS_SEEN_MS_AGO]);
 	if (bss[NL80211_BSS_LAST_SEEN_BOOTTIME]) {
-		u64 boottime;
+		u64 boottime, now, age;
 		struct timespec ts;
 
 #ifndef CLOCK_BOOTTIME
@@ -866,11 +866,18 @@
 		if (clock_gettime(CLOCK_BOOTTIME, &ts) == 0) {
 			/* Use more accurate boottime information to update the
 			 * scan result age since the driver reports this and
-			 * CLOCK_BOOTTIME is available. */
+			 * CLOCK_BOOTTIME is available. The kernel stamps the
+			 * machine's boot clock, which a time namespace offsets
+			 * from ours, so the kernel's own age stands whenever
+			 * the two disagree by more than a second. */
 			boottime = nla_get_u64(
 				bss[NL80211_BSS_LAST_SEEN_BOOTTIME]);
-			r->age = ((u64) ts.tv_sec * 1000000000 +
-				  ts.tv_nsec - boottime) / 1000000;
+			now = (u64) ts.tv_sec * 1000000000 + ts.tv_nsec;
+			age = (now - boottime) / 1000000;
+			if (now >= boottime &&
+			    (!bss[NL80211_BSS_SEEN_MS_AGO] ||
+			     (age + 1000 >= r->age && age <= r->age + 1000ULL)))
+				r->age = age;
 		}
 	}
 	r->ie_len = ie_len;
